# PowerShell shell (Windows)

This repo’s agent shell is **PowerShell**. Do **not** use bash-only constructs.

## Forbidden (bash-only)

- Heredoc: `$(cat <<'EOF' ... EOF)`
- Unquoted git upstream: `@{u}` (PowerShell parses `@{...}` as a hashtable)
- Bash arrays / `export FOO=bar` style assuming bash

## Use instead

### Multi-line commit / PR body

```powershell
git commit -m @"
type(scope): subject

body
"@

$body = @"
## Summary
- item

## Test plan
- [ ] item
"@
gh pr create --title "type(scope): subject" --body $body
```

### Upstream / tracking

```powershell
git rev-parse --abbrev-ref --symbolic-full-name '@{u}'
git status -sb
```

### Chaining

Prefer `;` between independent commands. Use separate Shell calls when a failure must stop the sequence.

### Paths

Prefer repo-relative or full Windows paths. Quoting paths with spaces is required.

## Reminder

User-facing commit rules still follow Conventional Commits (`.cursor/rules/conventional-commits.mdc`). Only the **shell syntax** for creating the commit differs on Windows.
